From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GoProSlowYo <68455785+goproslowyo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:25:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] dndcp: Map a layer shell overlay for a native Wayland
 drag

A host to guest drag is an XDND drag from the detection window, a Gtk
window on the x11 backend, because GDK is pinned to that backend process
wide. Under a Wayland session the window is an Xwayland client, and
whether its drag reaches a native Wayland application depends on the
compositor. KWin and Mutter bridge an X11 drag to Wayland clients, and
wlroots does not. That is wlroots issue #841. On sway every drop onto a
Wayland application was lost, six times out of six. The source logged
drag-begin and the target saw nothing, while the same drag onto an
Xwayland target succeeded. A plain Gtk drag source on the x11 backend
behaves the same with open-vm-tools absent, so the limit is in the
compositor.

A wl_data_device drag is core protocol, and reaches native clients on
wlroots, KWin and Mutter alike. A client can start one only from the
serial of a button press on a surface of its own, and it is not told
where the pointer is. This patch adds the first half of waylandDrag/,
which provides those surfaces. It keeps its own connection to
WAYLAND_DISPLAY, as waylandClipboard/ does, and binds
wl_data_device_manager and zwlr_layer_shell_v1. WaylandDrag_Arm() copies
the formats to offer and maps a transparent layer shell overlay over
each output, so that a press anywhere lands on one of them. An output
that goes away is dropped with its overlay. Where layer shell is absent,
as on GNOME, WaylandDrag_Init() fails, and it does not ask such a
compositor again.

Waits for the compositor stop at a deadline and never iterate the
caller's main loop, which also carries the RPC channel. Iterating it
would dispatch RPC commands from inside an RPC handler.

Offer only the formats that have bytes. A wl_data_source.send can only
end in a closed pipe, so serving nothing for an offered type reads at
the other end as a successful transfer of zero bytes. GTK turns an empty
text/uri-list into a NULL vector rather than an empty one, and libfm
walks that vector without checking it, so PCManFM crashes on an offer
with nothing behind it. WaylandDrag_Arm() drops such formats and fails
if none remain, which leaves the drag to XDND.

wlr-layer-shell is not part of wayland-protocols, so its XML from
wlr-protocols is added next to its user, and the protocol code is
generated from it when the plugin is built. The XML refers to xdg_popup,
so the xdg-shell interface code is generated too. The next patch starts
the drag, and the one after it uses the module.
